sesmesh in US-SOMO
==================

This directory holds sesmesh, a mesher for the solvent-excluded surface (SES) of a
set of spheres, from https://github.com/ehb54/sesmesh at commit 108de64 (2026-11-14,
"Merge pull request #5 from ehb54/progress-cancel").  The files are unchanged.

  src/          the sesmesh sources: ses, mesh, clean, parallel, vec3 (the mesher),
                io (its file writers), sesmesh.cpp (the command-line program), and
                coalesce, rcoal_io, fortio.h and rcoal.cpp (its C++ port of BEST's
                mesh coarsener rcoal)
  README.md     sesmesh's README: method, options and validation
  LICENSE       sesmesh's MIT license (it also names rcoal's author)

sesmesh is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE), so it can be built into US-SOMO.


How SOMO builds and uses it
---------------------------

libus_somo.pro compiles only the mesher, src/{ses,mesh,clean,parallel}.cpp, into the
library.  SOMO writes the .bod file itself, so io, which also needs the rcoal port, is
not built; the other files are kept only to mirror sesmesh's tree (sesmesh.cpp and
rcoal.cpp hold programs' main()s).  SOMO includes the headers by path
("../sesmesh/src/ses.h"); src/ is not on the include path, because src/io.h would
hide the system <io.h> on Windows.  sesmesh needs C++14 or later, so libus_somo.pro
sets CONFIG += c++17.

When "Compute on the solvent-excluded surface of the bead model" is checked in the
ZENO options, US_Hydrodyn_Zeno::run (src/us_hydrodyn_zeno.cpp) takes the bead
centres and radii as the spheres, meshes their SES with the probe radius and grid
spacing set there (cleaned up, cavities filled, unless unchecked), and writes the
triangles to the .bod file as TRIANGLE lines instead of one SPHERE line per bead.
sesmesh runs on as many threads as ZENO (SOMO's thread setting).  It reports its
progress to the progress bar, and Stop ends it (sesmesh's progress functions);
Visualize Bead Model, which meshes the beads it shows, does the same.


Updating
--------

Copy src/*.{h,cpp}, README.md and LICENSE from a newer sesmesh commit, update the
commit above, and check that the mesher's files in libus_somo.pro (and what they
include) still match src/.
